{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1174961-disciplines-to-contracts-1e","id":1174961,"title":"Disciplines to contracts 1E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-10T13:13:33-08:00","id":1174961,"title":"Disciplines to contracts 1E","content":"I have a character that was curious if you could convert disciplines from vampire the requiem into contracts for first edition changeling the lost. I believe he\u2019s interested in auspex or dominate. Not sure if I could convert them into contracts and even then I would not know how to go about it. Any ideas On how to go about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T15:15:42-08:00","id":1174997,"title":"","content":"Converting Disciplines to Contracts is a larger undertaking. First, did you ask your player if they would be satisfied with pre-existing Contracts? There's actually a large selection:<br /> <br /> Contracts of Communion - Large overlap with Auspex, but flavored with a chosen &quot;element&quot;.<br /> Contracts of Fleeting [Season] - First Dot of each reveals something about target's motivation.<br /> <br /> Contracts of Omen (Vision of Strife) - Reveals target's worst memory.<br /> Contracts of Potential (Light the Path) - Learn target's current motivation.<br /> Contracts of Potential (Read the Web) - Understand the nature of a relationship between two targets.<br /> Contracts of Potential (Shift the Foundation) - Temporarily modify target's Virtue or Vice.<br /> Contracts of Reflection (Reflections of the Past) - Review what has been reflected in an object during the last week.<br /> Goblin Contract (The Blessing of Forgetfulness) - Deletes one of target's memories, but you botch an important Subterfuge roll.<br /> Goblin Contract (Diviner's Madness) - See past or future of the subject, but you get unhinged and you need someone to remember it for you.<br /> Goblin Contract (Sight of Truth and Lies) - You become a living lie detector, but you're forbidden to lie during that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T18:49:11-08:00","id":1175056,"title":"","content":"Well he\u2019s wanting to play a lovecraftian type with mental powers. Changeling 1E has several mind altering effects but when it comes to making a full on psychic the contracts can be a bit underwhelming. I don\u2019t think an auspex conversion would be very difficult or overpowere, but I\u2019m not sure about dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T08:20:21-08:00","id":1175175,"title":"","content":"I'm more of a vampire guy than Changeling, at least until 2e comes out and I can better educate myself, so I'll approach your question from that perspective.<br /> <br /> Auspex is a versatile investigative tool. It's very efficient for what it gives you in a package. <br /> Dominate is a versatile and exceptionally powerful/efficient mental package.<br /> <br /> Players tend to home in, however, on one or another aspect of the package--if they used the whole as effectively as is possible, you'd be worrying mainly about reigning them in! Or, you'd be thinking like a Mage storyteller.... So, with that in mind it would help to clarify what, in your estimation or knowledge, your PC would want to do with his mental powers?<br /> <br /> Note, by the way, that a Lovecraftian approach to powers applied through Changeling Contracts works perfectly: contact with elder things and bending reality through the unfathomable, and all that. But, given that vampires are the princes of efficient packages, a Changeling will probably have to split what even a given dot-level power would do into several Contracts, hinging on circumstances to a greater extent.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T11:38:35-08:00","id":1175240,"title":"","content":"He seems to be most interested in the ability to command a person in A subtle way, But he is also very interested in the idea of slowly brainwashing someone into a servant.At first I thought it would be a simple matter of just changing a few names and applying glamour costs to each power, but even the low level abilities same stronger than most contracts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T04:26:21-08:00","id":1175419,"title":"","content":"Can I ask what you mean by &quot;lovecraftian type&quot; here? Normally, that's associated more with hallicinations and madness, often fear, and a healthy dose of body horror. I don't understand the link between Dominate/Auspex and Lovecraft here. Are you talking about just playing a psychic powers type?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-12-2018, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T06:44:36-08:00","id":1175443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1174961-disciplines-to-contracts-1e?p=1175240#post1175240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He seems to be most interested in the ability to command a person in A subtle way, But he is also very interested in the idea of slowly brainwashing someone into a servant.At first I thought it would be a simple matter of just changing a few names and applying glamour costs to each power, but even the low level abilities same stronger than most contracts</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly? This can already be done through Changeling lucid dream powers and decent character skills--no Contract needed. He'd basically spend time dream-gaslighting someone until their perspectives change sufficiently. You could make an extended series of social maneuvering tests to reflect resistance and/or simple process (things CAN go wrong...). <br /> <br /> So is Dominate stronger than Changeling powers of perception alteration and control? No! It's quicker, more blatant and ... crude. Dominate can do in two rounds what might take the Changeling two months of effort, but the end result for the Changeling will be more stable and reliable. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T09:16:57-08:00","id":1175476,"title":"","content":"I had not really thought about it like that. I will bring this up with player. If we keep the powers subtle we could have something more like the curious case of Charles dexter Ward instead of just Dungeons &amp; Dragons style power gaming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T10:20:33-08:00","id":1175494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1174961-disciplines-to-contracts-1e?p=1175476#post1175476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had not really thought about it like that. I will bring this up with player. If we keep the powers subtle we could have something more like the curious case of Charles dexter Ward instead of just Dungeons &amp; Dragons style power gaming</div> </div> </div> </div>Vamps are scary because within six seconds you'll be doing what they want you to do, exactly, and not remember a thing. Changelings are scary because within six nights you'd sell your soul and your family's innocent flesh for a good sleep, and remember <i>everything</i>.<br /> <br /> Which one does he want to be?<br /> <br /> IMO you can do Lovecraft with vamps, but it gets harder than when your supernatural base already transits dimensions of strange skies and plumbs the depths of your defenseless subconscious every time your body shuts down for repairs. Mage, of course, can do all this too, but Mage can do literally anything--by design.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. For fun, look up the effects of sleep-deprivation as well. Also, note that sod-normal humans spend Willpower all the time because their dice pools are low and they get 1 point/day. If they don't get the refill point, however....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}